# The build context is this directory now, not a single service's, so every
# pattern has to be written to match at any depth. [F-6] #76.
#
# **`**/` is load-bearing on every line.** A bare `.env` matches only
# `backend/.env` — Docker anchors an unprefixed pattern at the context root.
# While each service built from its own directory that was the same thing; once
# the context moved up, `backend/market_service/.env` stopped being excluded
# and went straight into the image. It is gitignored precisely because it holds
# a real DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET, so a pattern that silently narrowed put
# the signing key in a published layer. Anything added below gets `**/` unless
# there is a stated reason it should match the root alone.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Each service keeps a local virtualenv here for running its suite. Without
# this an image build ships a second copy of every dependency it just
# pip-installed.
**/.venv/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/

# Tests are not part of a runtime image.
**/unit_test/

# `shared/testing.py` is test plumbing too — it is the one module of the shared
# package no service imports at runtime, so it has no business in a production
# layer. Named explicitly rather than by a pattern, because a glob over the
# shared package would be a trap the next person adding a module walks into.
shared/testing.py

**/*.db
